# NON-SECRET per-environment container sizing config for the production host
# (Lightsail medium_3_0, 4GB). The deploy seeds these into /srv/footbag/env
# keyed on FOOTBAG_ENV; this committed file is the source of truth, so the
# production sizing no longer depends on an operator remembering to set it.
#
# Secrets (session, origin-verify, internal-event, API/webhook keys) live in
# /srv/footbag/env (operator-managed) and AWS SSM, NEVER here. Never add a
# secret, API key, identity, hostname, or URL to this file.
#
# Production sets the x264 preset rather than taking the libx264 default of
# medium. Both hosts have two vCPUs, so production is no faster at encoding than
# staging, and at medium the encoder cannot finish a file at the accepted size
# limit inside its time budget: measured on 720p material at two threads, medium
# runs 3.6x realtime against faster's 7.0x, which on this host is the difference
# between roughly 68 MB and roughly 134 MB of accepted video. Running medium
# here would leave the advertised limit failing at the top of its own range.
#
# 'faster' rather than staging's 'veryfast' keeps more compression efficiency
# while still clearing the limit with margin. Raising the accepted size beyond
# the current default means revisiting this preset, the ffmpeg time budget and
# the caller deadline together, not any one of them alone.

NGINX_MEMORY_LIMIT=128M
WEB_MEMORY_LIMIT=512M
WORKER_MEMORY_LIMIT=384M
IMAGE_MEMORY_LIMIT=896M
IMAGE_MAX_CONCURRENT=2
VIDEO_X264_PRESET=faster
